    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`, returned on the owner read flow (`GET`/`POST /api/owners`).\n\nI followed the codebase's established convention for derived owner fields (locality, membershipLevel, bulkSignupWarning, etc.), which keeps structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New cohesive unit** \u2014 `OwnerContactPreferencePolicy.java`: a tiny final class with one simple static method (CC\u22482, no surrounding context to hold \u2014 `WMC_other`\u22480). Modeled directly on the existing `OwnerLocalityPolicy`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line wiring the policy into `toOwnerDto` (the interface method itself is CC=1, one changed line).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `contactPreference` read-only property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nNo existing method grew in complexity, and no large class was edited beyond a single annotation line \u2014 the biggest lever (`WMC_other` of a big class) is avoided by putting the logic in its own single-method class.",
